---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<LegalLayout title="Privacy policy" description="What this site collects and what happens to it." updated="6 October 2026">
  <p>This is my personal portfolio. The site doesn't collect anything about you on purpose.</p>

  <h2>What I collect</h2>
  <p>Nothing through the site itself. There's no contact form, no analytics, no tracking pixels and no advertising cookies. The only thing the site saves is your choice on the Pause motion button, so it's remembered next time. That stays in your own browser and never reaches me.</p>
  <p>If you email me, I get your email address and whatever you write.</p>

  <h2>Who handles it</h2>
  <p>The site is hosted by Vercel, which is based in the United States. Like any web host, Vercel sees your IP address when a page loads and keeps short-lived server logs. The fonts load from Google Fonts, so Google sees your IP address too, as with most websites.</p>

  <h2>What I do with it</h2>
  <p>If you email me, I read it and reply. I don't add you to a mailing list, share your details or sell them.</p>

  <h2>Seeing, fixing or deleting your details</h2>
  <p>Email me at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and I'll send you what I hold, correct it or delete it.</p>

  <h2>Complaints</h2>
  <p>If something's wrong, email me first and I'll sort it out. If you're not happy with my answer, you can contact the <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/privacy/privacy-complaints">Office of the Australian Information Commissioner</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
